    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #155\n\n- 2026-09-11 13:51Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-11 14:12Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #380 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-155-generic-rest-05-09-expose-view-crud-an-thr_97iw45ky5r` to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #155: exposes the view endpoint family over the generic REST layer as thin mappings onto the choke-point's existing view/view_items services. - `POST /api/databases/:id/views`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/views/:id`, `PUT/DELETE /api/views/:id/items/:itemId` — all in `backend/services/semprec-api/src/viewsHandler.ts`, wired into `app.ts`. - Added a live item-existence check to `chokePoint.addViewItem` (view_items carries no FK to the partitioned `items` table) so an unknown item id in the `PUT` route answers `not_found` deterministically, per the acceptance criteria. - Exported `Actor` from `@semprec/data` so the adapter can type it; every write here uses `{ type: 'user' }` since this REST surface only authenticates human sessions (agent-actor writes go through a different adapter, per the existing ADR excluding views from the agent-proposal flow). - Extended `routeMatrix.ts` and `chokePointWriteBoundary.unit.test.ts` with the 5 new routes. - New `viewsHandler.test.ts` (16 tests): create/patch/delete, curated add/reposition/remove, PUT idempotence, and 404s for unknown view/item on both PUT and DELETE, plus a 400 for adding to a non-curated view. Verified: backend's full `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 992 unit/integration tests, dependency-boundary checks, 5 e2e tests) and web's full `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 139 tests) both pass with no regressions. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 14:44Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #380 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Working tree is clean — no new changes to commit. Commit `c7b5b98` (the TOCTOU fix) was already pushed earlier in this conversation, and `git push` confirms origin is already up to date. ## Summary Branch `bb/relay-155-generic-rest-05-09-expose-view-crud-an-thr_97iw45ky5r` is pushed to origin and up to date with all work for issue #155. Implements the view endpoint family as thin choke-point mappings: - `POST /api/databases/:id/views`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/views/:id` - `PUT/DELETE /api/views/:id/items/:itemId` for curated view membership (add, reposition, remove) Addressed all 4 findings from the automated code review on PR #380: fixed a real TOCTOU gap (`deleteView`/`removeViewItem` now throw `not_found` instead of silently no-op'ing on a raced delete), and replied in-thread on the other two findings, which were already covered by existing choke-point behavior (config validation, actor/ownership model) rather than needing new code. Full verification passed on both workspaces: `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit, boundary checks, integration, e2e) and `web/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, tests) — no failures. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 15:21Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #380 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Working tree was clean; commit `5167a23` (this round's review-response fixes) was already made and is now pushed to origin. ## Summary Branch `bb/relay-155-generic-rest-05-09-expose-view-crud-an-thr_97iw45ky5r` is pushed to origin with all work for issue #155. Implements the view endpoint family as thin choke-point mappings: `POST /api/databases/:id/views`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/views/:id`, and `PUT/DELETE /api/views/:id/items/:itemId` for curated view membership (add, reposition, remove). This round addressed the latest code-review findings on PR #380: - Fixed `chokePoint.removeViewItem` silently no-op'ing on a non-member `itemId` — it now throws `NotFoundError`, matching the pattern already applied to `deleteView`/`addViewItem`/`reorderViewItem`. - Fixed unvalidated `position` input on the membership `PUT` route — now rejects non-integer/negative values with a 400 instead of letting them fail as an unhandled 500 against Postgres's `integer` column. - Replied in-thread (no code change) to a finding asking for per-item access control on `addViewItem`'s existence check — this codebase has no per-item ACL model anywhere, so the same \"gap\" already exists on every `GET` item/database route; a real fix belongs in its own issue applied consistently, not bolted onto this one endpoint. Full verification passed on both workspaces after these fixes: `backend/pnpm run verify` (204 unit + 994 integration + 5 e2e tests) and `web/pnpm run verify` (139 tests) — no failures. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 15:50Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #380 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Working tree was clean; commit `e9fa153` (this round's review fixes) was already made and is now pushed to origin. ## Summary Branch `bb/relay-155-generic-rest-05-09-expose-view-crud-an-thr_97iw45ky5r` is pushed to origin with all work for issue #155. Implements the view endpoint family as thin choke-point mappings: `POST /api/databases/:id/views`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/views/:id`, and `PUT/DELETE /api/views/:id/items/:itemId` for curated view membership (add, reposition, remove). This round addressed the two remaining findings from PR #380's review: - `DELETE /api/views/:id/items/:itemId` now rejects a linked (non-curated) view with the same 400 `ValidationError` `PUT` already used, instead of masking it as a misleading 404. - `position` on the membership `PUT` route is now capped at Postgres's `integer` max, rejecting an out-of-range value with a 400 instead of letting it surface as an unhandled 500. Full verification passed on both workspaces: `backend/pnpm run verify` (204 unit + 995 integration + 5 e2e tests) and `web/pnpm run verify` (139 tests) — no failures. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 16:16Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #380 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Working tree was already clean; the commit from